\DOC ADD_IBT_TAC

\TYPE {ADD_IBT_TAC : thm -> thm -> thm -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a correctness goal about a full machine-code program by deriving it from
a theorem stated for the corresponding trimmed program.

\DESCRIBE
{fullmc} is a theorem giving the byte-list definition of the full machine code,
{trimc} the analogous definition of the trimmed machine code, and {th} an
already-proved specification theorem whose statement coincides with the goal
except that it mentions the trimmed code in place of the full code. Applied to
a goal whose conclusion is a universally quantified (sometimes existentially
prefixed) {ensures} specification mentioning the full machine-code constant, it
discharges the goal completely:
{
       A ?- t
   ======================  ADD_IBT_TAC fullmc trimc th
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, only this closing behaviour appears, on goals with no
assumptions whose conclusions are machine-code correctness statements paired
with a matching specification theorem for the trimmed code.

\ENDDOC
